     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Second switch of the new-idle balancing change that introduced NI_RANDOM (default on). The kernel source documents only NI_RANDOM, so what this one does exactly is not described there: treat it as an experimental on/off toggle and leave it at its default unless a measured run says otherwise."),
     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "The HRTICK idea for SCHED_DEADLINE entities: arm a high-resolution timer for the exact end of a deadline runtime budget instead of waiting for the next tick (default on where the kernel was built with deferred hrtimer rearm, otherwise off). It only matters when something runs under SCHED_DEADLINE, which is rare on a desktop."),
     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Off by default; the kernel source has no comment on it, and by its name it concerns the average-virtual-runtime bookkeeping that EEVDF's eligibility test rests on. Not a tuning knob: it is listed so the whole feature list is visible and is never part of a calibration or autotune decision."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Cache-aware scheduling: length of the epoch over which a process's cache occupancy per LLC is accumulated before it is re-evaluated (the kernel reports it in its own unit; stock 3). Shorter reacts faster to a process changing its working set but flips its preferred LLC more often; longer is steadier. The kernel source has little commentary on it. Needs CONFIG_SCHED_CACHE."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Cache-aware scheduling: how many epochs a process keeps its preferred-LLC assignment before that preference may be dropped when its cache use no longer points there (stock 5). Larger = stickier placement of a game's threads on one CCD, smaller = quicker release. The kernel source has little commentary on it. Needs CONFIG_SCHED_CACHE."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "NUMA balancing, How much address space (MB) one NUMA-balancing scan pass unmaps to sample page locality. Larger samples faster but costs more page faults. This machine has one NUMA node and kernel.numa_balancing is 0, so the value changes nothing here; the row exists so the whole scheduler is visible. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "NUMA balancing, Shortest interval (ms) between scans of one task; the scanner speeds up towards it while the task keeps faulting remote pages. This machine has one NUMA node and kernel.numa_balancing is 0, so the value changes nothing here; the row exists so the whole scheduler is visible. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "NUMA balancing, Longest interval (ms) between scans of one task; the scanner slows down towards it once the task's pages are local. This machine has one NUMA node and kernel.numa_balancing is 0, so the value changes nothing here; the row exists so the whole scheduler is visible. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "NUMA balancing, How long (ms) a new task runs before its first scan. This machine has one NUMA node and kernel.numa_balancing is 0, so the value changes nothing here; the row exists so the whole scheduler is visible. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "NUMA balancing, Memory tiering only: a page counts as hot when it faults again within this many ms, which makes it a candidate for promotion to the fast tier. This machine has one NUMA node and kernel.numa_balancing is 0, so the value changes nothing here; the row exists so the whole scheduler is visible. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Upper bound (ns) of the time-slice extension a user thread may request through rseq: a thread inside a short critical section can ask to finish it before being preempted. Stock 5000. 0 effectively refuses the request. Only matters for programs that use the extension; the kernel clamps what it accepts, so a rejected value is reported by the write."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "How many microseconds per sched_rt_period_us real-time tasks (SCHED_FIFO/RR) may run before being throttled so normal tasks cannot starve. -1 or a value equal to the period = no throttle (what this system has). Lowering it protects the desktop from a runaway real-time thread, at the cost of capping real-time audio and input threads. Never part of a calibration: a halved value would throttle them."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Time slice (ms) of SCHED_RR real-time tasks of equal priority before the next one runs. Stock 100. Only affects programs that run threads in SCHED_RR; ordinary and SCHED_FIFO tasks ignore it."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "On a page fault in a file-backed mapping (program text, shared libraries, mmapped game assets) the kernel also maps up to this many bytes of neighbouring pages that are already in the page cache (stock 65536; a power of two, at least the page size). Larger = fewer minor faults when memory is read sequentially, at the price of mapping pages that may never be touched; smaller = the opposite."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "x86 TLB flush policy: when a range is not larger than this many pages the kernel invalidates the pages one by one, above it flushes the whole TLB (stock 33). Higher keeps unrelated translations cached on larger ranges but spends more instructions per flush; lower flushes everything sooner. Small effect, visible mostly in heavy munmap or mprotect loads."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Laptop mode batches disk writes: while it is non-zero the kernel delays writeback and flushes everything at once whenever a read has spun the disk up anyway (the value is how long, in seconds, dirty data may wait; 0 = off). Meant for spinning disks; on an SSD it only makes writeback bursty. Interacts with vm.dirty_writeback_centisecs and vm.dirty_expire_centisecs. This system has it at 2."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "When memory runs out: 0 = the OOM killer scans every task and kills the one with the worst score, 1 = it kills the task that triggered the allocation without scanning. 1 is quicker on machines with very many tasks but can kill an innocent small process. Behaviour, not performance: never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Kernel Samepage Merging: when on, pages that are entirely zero are merged with the kernel's shared zero page even when they are not otherwise identical to a merge candidate. Has no effect while KSM is off (mm.ksm_run = 0, as here). Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Kernel Samepage Merging: when on, the scanner skips pages it has repeatedly failed to merge, so it spends its pages_to_scan budget on pages that can still merge. Has no effect while KSM is off (mm.ksm_run = 0, as here). Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Memory tiering only: the most MB per second NUMA balancing may promote from the slow memory tier to the fast one (stock 65536). Without a second memory tier, as on this laptop, nothing is promoted and the value changes nothing. Never part of a calibration."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "mac80211's Airtime Queue Limit caps how much transmit airtime one station may have queued in the driver, so a slow client cannot fill the queue and add latency for all others. 1 = on (stock), 0 = off, only useful to compare against. Present only while a mac80211 Wi-Fi driver such as mt76 is loaded."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Airtime queue limit threshold (microseconds of airtime, stock 24000): once the whole interface has more than this queued, the per-station limit tightens. Lower = lower latency under load, higher = more queued data for throughput. Present only while a mac80211 Wi-Fi driver is loaded."),
+    QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "mt76 Wi-Fi driver: 1 = receive processing runs in its own kernel thread that the scheduler can place and prioritise, 0 = in the softirq on the interrupted CPU. A thread isolates network load from the cores a game uses; softirq has lower per-packet overhead. Present only with an mt76 adapter."),
     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Kernel 6.6+: how widely an unbound work item may travel from the CPU that queued it. cache (stock) = within the same L3 - on a two-CCD Ryzen the work stays on the die that asked for it, no cross-CCD cache traffic; smt / cpu = even closer (better locality, less work-conservation); numa / system = anywhere (best for spreading heavy work, worst locality). Use together with 'Unbound workqueue CPUs', which is a hard CPU mask; this row is only the locality preference inside that mask."),
     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Confines every unbound kernel workqueue (writeback, crypto, most filesystem background work) to the CPUs of one CCD, keeping that background work off whichever CCD the game runs on. Typical use: set this to 'frequency' (or whichever CCD is NOT hosting the game) while the Game launch tab's affinity points the game at 'cache'/the V-Cache CCD - filesystem/crypto work then physically cannot preempt or share L2/L3 with the game's threads. Pick 'all' to undo (kernel default spreads across every CPU). Only offered with 2+ CCDs; a single-CCD chip has nothing to confine work away from."),
     QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("OptimizationBackend", "Sets smp_affinity_list for every IRQ to one CCD's CPUs, so device interrupts (network, USB, most peripherals) fire on cores the game is not using. Same pairing idea as workqueue CPUs above: point this at the non-gaming CCD. Best-effort by design - multi-queue NVMe/network IRQs are often kernel-managed and refuse a manual affinity change (reported as 'refused', not a failure); single-CPU-only IRQs (per-CPU timers) are skipped since they say nothing about policy either way. 'all' restores the kernel's default spread. A running irqbalance daemon would undo the setting within seconds: it is stopped while a CCD is set and started again on restore or 'all' (only if Centurion stopped it)."),
